3. Examples of Individual Use

The following are Individual Use:

  a. learning a subject for Your own interest or career;
  b. studying as a student, including for coursework You choose to use the
     Software on;
  c. research You design and conduct Yourself, including studies with
     participants You recruit and run, and publishing the results, even if the
     research counts toward a degree or a supervisor suggested the Software;
  d. a teacher using the Software to prepare their own material, or
     suggesting it to students as an optional aid;
  e. an employee learning a subject for their own knowledge or career, even
     if the subject relates to their job, provided the employer does not
     require or direct the use and the Software is not used to perform work
