4. Examples of Organizational Use

The following are Organizational Use and require a separate license:

  a. requiring the Software for a course, or including it in official
     curriculum or course materials;
  b. installing, hosting, or providing the Software to students, staff,
     members, or customers on behalf of an Organization;
  c. use by a laboratory, research group, or department as a shared tool, or
     in studies it runs as a group;
  d. use by or for a company in its business, including in products,
     services, required or internal training, or work performed for it;
  e. offering paid instruction, training, or services built on the Software.

If a use matches examples in both section 3 and this section, it is
Organizational Use.

